.TH ZERODDS-WS-BRIDGED 1 "" "ZeroDDS" "ZeroDDS Manual"
.SH NAME
zerodds-ws-bridged \- DDS to WebSocket bridge daemon
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B zerodds-ws-bridged
[\fB\-\-config\fR \fIFILE\fR]
[\fB\-\-listen\fR \fIADDR\fR]
[\fB\-\-domain\fR \fIID\fR]
[\fB\-\-topic\fR \fINAME\fR[:\fIWS_PATH\fR]]...
[\fB\-\-log\-level\fR \fILEVEL\fR]
[\fB\-\-metrics\fR \fIADDR\fR]
[\fB\-V\fR | \fB\-\-version\fR]
[\fB\-h\fR | \fB\-\-help\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B zerodds-ws-bridged
exposes selected DDS topics to WebSocket clients and forwards inbound WS
messages onto matching DDS publishers. It is the reference DDS \(<> WS
bridge for the ZeroDDS distribution and implements
.IR docs/specs/zerodds-ws-bridge-1.0.md .
.PP
The daemon reads the YAML file given with
.BR \-\-config ,
with drop-ins in its sibling
.IR FILE .d/;
without that option it reads the system file
.I /etc/zerodds/ws-bridged.yaml
with
.I /etc/zerodds/ws-bridged.d/
(on macOS under
.IR /usr/local/etc/zerodds )
when it exists, and the built-in defaults otherwise.
On Linux it integrates with
.BR systemd (1)
via Type=notify; on macOS with
.BR launchd (8);
on Windows it runs as service
.BR ZeroDDSWSBridge .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-\-config =\fIFILE\fR
Path to the YAML configuration. See
.BR zerodds-ws-bridged.yaml (5).
.TP
.BR \-\-listen =\fIADDR\fR
Bind address. Default:
.IR 127.0.0.1:8080 .
.TP
.BR \-\-domain =\fIID\fR
DDS domain id. Default: 0.
.TP
.BR \-\-topic =\fINAME\fR[:\fIWS_PATH\fR]
One more topic entry (repeatable): the DDS topic
.IR NAME ,
and behind the single
.I :
that is not part of a
.I ::
the path of its WebSocket endpoint, which begins with
.IR / .
Without
.I WS_PATH
the path is
.IR /topics/<slug-of-name> .
.I \-\-topic Chat::Message:/chat
serves
.I Chat::Message
at
.IR /chat .
.TP
.BR \-\-tls\-cert =\fIFILE\fR
TLS cert (PEM); enables
.IR wss:// .
.TP
.BR \-\-tls\-key =\fIFILE\fR
TLS key (PEM).
.TP
.BR \-\-auth\-token =\fISECRET\fR
Bearer token auth.
.TP
.BR \-\-log\-level =\fILEVEL\fR
Override the configured log level. One of
.IR trace ", " debug ", " info ", " warn ", " error .
Default:
.IR info .
The log is one JSON object per line on stdout, with
.IR timestamp ", " level ", " event
and the fields of the event, such as
.IR connection_id ", " topic ", " bytes ", " peer ", " latency_us ;
a frame in or out is an event of level
.IR debug .
An error that ends the start is written to stderr as well.
.TP
.BR \-\-metrics =\fIADDR\fR
Prometheus scrape endpoint.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the program name and the version of the crate.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print full option synopsis.
.TP
.BR \-\-set " \fIPATH\fR=\fIVALUE\fR"
One setting above every file, repeatable;
.BI + PATH = VALUE
appends to a list.
.TP
.B \-\-check\-config
Validate and print the effective configuration with the origin of every
value, then exit: 0 valid, 1 invalid value or unknown key, 2 unreadable
file, syntax error or include cycle.
.SH SIGNALS
.TP
.B SIGTERM
Graceful shutdown within
.B shutdown_drain_ms
(default 30 s): no new connection, the samples the daemon holds reach the
clients, every connection gets
.I {"op":"shutdown"}
and a Close frame with status 1001, then the DDS entities are removed and the
process exits 0.
.TP
.B SIGHUP
Reads the configuration again: the TLS certificate and key files at their
configured paths, the auth settings and the topic ACL apply from then on
(the certificate to new connections; a connection keeps its session).
Changed TLS file paths, topics, limits, origin, metrics,
max_send_queue_per_connection, max_burst_samples, ping_interval_ms,
shutdown_drain_ms, catalog_on_connect, tenants (other than the acl of a tenant's topic), listen address or
domain need a restart and are logged; a changed
log_level applies at once. A configuration
that does not load changes nothing.
.SH WINDOWS SERVICE
Started by the service control manager, the daemon runs as the service
.BR ZeroDDSWSBridge :
start pending until it serves, then running; the stop and shutdown
controls are SIGTERM,
.B sc.exe control ZeroDDSWSBridge paramchange
is SIGHUP; when it ends, the service is stopped with the exit status below.
Started from a console, Ctrl+C, Ctrl+Break and the closing of the console
are SIGTERM.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT
Optional OTLP endpoint, such as http://localhost:4318. When it is set, the
daemon sends OTLP/HTTP/JSON spans to its
.I /v1/traces
every 5 s and at the end of a shutdown: one trace per WebSocket connection
with the root
.BR ws.connection ,
a
.B ws.frame.in
per message of the client (with the child
.B dds.write
when it wrote into DDS) and a
.B ws.frame.out
per message of the daemon.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Normal shutdown (SIGTERM/SIGINT).
.TP
.B 1
Configuration error.
.TP
.B 2
Bind error \(em address in use.
.TP
.B 3
DDS error \(em the participant does not start.
.TP
.B 4
TLS error \(em the certificate or the key does not load.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/zerodds/ws-bridged.yaml
Suggested deployment path, loaded only when selected with
.BR \-\-config .
Documented in
.BR zerodds-ws-bridged.yaml (5).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR zerodds-ws-bridged.yaml (5),
.BR zerodds-mqtt-bridged (1),
.BR zerodds-admin (1),
.BR systemd.service (5).
.SH STANDARDS
DDS 1.4, RTPS 2.5, XTypes 1.3, RFC 6455 (WebSocket), RFC 7692 (permessage-deflate).
